          <a class="btn btn-primary btn-sm" href={href('quickstart/')}
            >Get started <span class="arr">→</span></a
          >
        </div>
      </header>

      <!-- ===================== Hero ===================== -->
      <section class="hero">
        <div class="container hero-grid">
          <div class="hero-copy">
            <p class="vx-kicker">// a task runner and cache for JavaScript monorepos</p>
            <h1>Hundreds of commands.<br /><span class="phosphor">Which must run?</span></h1>
            <p class="lede">
              A monorepo's build is hundreds of commands across its packages. Which of them must run,
              in what order, and which can be skipped because their result is already known? vx is a
              task runner that answers from what each task declares, and stores each result under a
              key made from its inputs.
            </p>
            <div class="actions">
              <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href={href('learn/what-is-task-orchestration/')}
                >Learn how it works <span class="arr">→</span></a
              >
              <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href={href('learn/playground/')}
                >Plan a monorepo in your browser</a
              >
              <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href={href('quickstart/')}>Quickstart</a>
            </div>
            <div class="actions">
              <button class="install-pill" data-copy="npm install -g @vzn/vx" type="button">
                <span class="dollar">$</span>
                <span class="cmd">npm install -g @vzn/vx</span>
