                  ><span class="term-time">252ms</span><span class="term-time-rest"
                    > · max {termMax}ms · avg {termAvg}ms · min {termMin}ms</span
                  ></span
                >
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ===================== Idea 1: explicit inputs ===================== -->
      <section class="section" id="inputs">
        <div class="container idea-grid">
          <div class="idea-copy">
            <p class="vx-kicker">// idea 1 · explicit inputs</p>
            <h2>A key is only as honest as what it folds.</h2>
            <p class="sub">
              A cached result is replayed when its key matches. If a task reads a file its key never
              saw, an edit to that file still hits, and the run replays the old output: green, and
              wrong. vx folds what each task declares and infers nothing. The sandbox, opt-in per
              task, runs it where only the files it was granted exist, so an undeclared read fails the
              task, names the file and stores nothing.
            </p>
            <p class="guarantee">
              A test holds it: “<a href={`${GH}/blob/main/${guarantee.file}`}>{guarantee.row}</a>”, in
              core's <code>{guarantee.file.replace('packages/vx/', '')}</code>, which runs the stale-hit
